            <chunk name="Object" index="32">
              <items count="2">
                <item name="GUID" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">59e0b89a-e487-49f8-bab8-b5bab16be14c</item>
                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">7ac8de50-fde2-5164-a7da-fa7e721c209f</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">README</item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">TWISTED STAR TOWER (LOFT MASSING)

A star-shaped floor outline is made from a circle, filleted, copied up in floors and rotated a little more at each level; lofting the floors gives a twisting tower mass.

HOW TO USE
1. 'Star points' sets the number of star points; 'Star depth' how deep the star is cut in; 'Corner fillet' rounds the corners.
2. 'Floor height' and 'Floors' set the stacking; 'Twist per floor' is the extra rotation (degrees) of each level.
3. Loft options: the Value List picks the loft type; the toggle and 'Refit' adjust it.
4. Bake 'Loft' for the tower envelope, or the Rot3D output for the floor-plate outlines.

YOU WILL LEARN
- Alternating lists: Longest List repeats a short pattern (1, 0) over all points
- Amplitude: moving points along their own direction to make a star
- Series as floor heights and as rotation angles
- Loft and Loft Options

READ THE CANVAS LEFT TO RIGHT
Green = inputs you change, coloured boxes = numbered steps, blue = results.

SOURCE
Lucas Becker (runxel) - runxel/grasshopper-examples
gh/star_curve_loft.ghx @ 0e57586bdc
Licence: BlueOak-1.0.0 (see LICENCE panel)
Modified for the Almond parametric library: regrouped, relabelled and annotated; the geometric logic is unchanged.</item>
